# Thread-Safe LRU Cache in Rust

A clean approach: a `HashMap` for O(1) lookup plus a doubly linked list (implemented with index-based nodes in a slab, avoiding `Rc<RefCell<...>>` and unsafe pointers) to track recency. All state is guarded by a single `Mutex`.

```rust
use std::collections::HashMap;
use std::hash::Hash;
use std::sync::Mutex;

struct Node<K, V> {
    key: K,
    value: V,
    prev: Option<usize>,
    next: Option<usize>,
}

pub struct LruCache<K, V> {
    capacity: usize,
    map: HashMap<K, usize>,
    nodes: Vec<Node<K, V>>,          // slab of nodes; free slots reused
    free: Vec<usize>,                // recycled slots
    head: Option<usize>,             // most recently used
    tail: Option<usize>,             // least recently used
}

